# {{.ProjectName}}

{{.AgentName}} — an agent on the [agent-base](https://github.com/tankdonut/agent-base) container image. All boot
logic (spec validation, config/MCP/plugin reconciliation, content
seeding, cron scheduling) lives in the base image; this repo contributes
content only: a `spec.json`, seed directories, and image-baked
automations.

## Quick start

Install agentctl once (the agent-base operator CLI):

```sh
# release binary (pick your arch; checksums: agentctl-SHA256SUMS)
curl -fsSL -o ~/bin/agentctl \
  https://github.com/tankdonut/agent-base/releases/download/{{.BaseTag}}/agentctl-linux-amd64
# or build from source
go install ./agent-base/cmd/agentctl   # from a clone of tankdonut/agent-base
```

Then:

```sh
agentctl secrets init   # agent/.env from agent/.env.example (+ generated gateway token)
agentctl secrets edit   # fill in real values (ZAI_API_KEY is required)
agentctl secrets check  # verify every required var is set
agentctl up             # build + start (podman or docker, auto-detected)
agentctl dev            # dev overlay: bind-mounted seed content, no rebuild
```

`./make.sh <command>` works as a shim for the same commands.

Gateway: <http://localhost:18789/healthz> — loopback-only,
token-authenticated when OPENCLAW_GATEWAY_TOKEN is set.

## Structure

| Path | Purpose |
| ---- | ------- |
| `.agentctl.yaml` | Optional agentctl config (engine, gateway_port); defaults apply while commented out |
| `agent/spec.json` | Declarative boot contract (fail-closed loader) |
| `agent/Dockerfile` | Thin project image: FROM agent-base + five COPY lines |
| `agent/.env` | Secrets (gitignored), created from `agent/.env.example` |
| `agent/automations/` | Cron jobs, image-baked (never bind-mounted) |
| `agent/workspace/`, `agent/skills/`, `knowledge/content/` | Seed content for the data volume |
| `compose.yml` / `compose.dev.yml` | Production service + dev overlay |
| `make.sh` | Thin shim over agentctl (`exec agentctl "$@"`) |

